  "injected_prompt": "MEASURABLE COMPOSITION PRIOR [archetype=reception_lounge]: Conversation-first lounge: define the rug/core area, then arrange all seats to face one shared focus. Open floor is the residual of a good arrangement, not a protected rectangle.\nCompose the room in this order and keep the order visible in your reasoning: (1) name the single shared focus; (2) define one conversation/enclosure group around it; (3) place the group as one coherent figure (mirrored axis where the archetype asks for it); (4) put peripheral accents in wall niches OUTSIDE the entrance-to-focus sightline; (5) only then draw circulation, as ONE shared entrance trunk that branches near each activity.\nThresholds that will be measured and can reject this candidate: furniture coverage 14-45% of floor; at least 3 enclosing seats sharing one focus; focus-distance CV <= 0.50; every seat within 55 deg of the focus; enclosure arc >= 120 deg; mirrored pair error <= 0.25 m; access-area overlap <= 0.10 m2; shared route trunk >= 0.28 of mean route length.\nDo NOT satisfy these by adding protected open-space rectangles, by spreading one route per object from the entrance, or by declaring prose about openness instead of arranging real inventory. A measured failure reports its repair_target: decomposition for sparse inventory, layout for poses/facing/symmetry, spatial for zones/areas/routes. Repair at that layer; moving coordinates cannot fix a sparse inventory.",
